homtom: adopt the bootloader frame, quiet LCD console by default

TTBL scans its splash out of 0x30400000-0x3043FBFF. The 6.1 Image is
inflated to 0x30008000-0x30650494 (bss to 0x30674048), so the decompressor
writes kernel .text (VA 0xC0400000-0xC043FBFF) into the visible buffer: the
coloured noise after the splash. setup_arch() then moved the LCD DMA to the
reserved buffer at 0x33F00000 without filling it (stale RAM), and the
console cleared it to black and drew the boot log (verbose default).

Decompressor (boot/compressed/misc.c, C, CONFIG_MACH_TOMTOMGO only):
 - Before inflating, copy the frame the LCD is scanning (LCDSADDR1/2) to
   0x33F00000, clean those D-cache lines and drain the write buffer, then
   point LCDSADDR1/2 at the copy. Same pixels, so the switch is invisible.
   Skipped when ENVID is off, the LCD already scans 0x33F00000, the size is
   0 or above 256 KiB, the source is outside RAM or overlaps the target, or
   the decompressor heap reaches 0x33F00000. Nothing is added to head.S.

Board file:
 - homtom_reserve(): if the LCD already scans 0x33F00000, set
   homtom_fb_adopted and leave the LCD registers alone. Otherwise (fallback)
   mask the stale buffer with a black TPAL overlay, then relocate as before.
 - homtom_map_io(): TPAL is no longer cleared there (ladder builds only);
   homtom_fbtext_init() clears it after drawing.
 - /sys/kernel/homtom_splash becomes readable (1 = muted). INFORM0=5 in
   map_io is unchanged.

homtom-fbtext.c:
 - Quiet by default. "homtom.verbose=1" (early_param) restores the old
   verbose console. The console is muted before register_console(), so the
   CON_PRINTBUFFER replay draws nothing. With an adopted frame no pixel is
   written; otherwise the built-in splash (pixel-identical to SPLASHW.BMP)
   is drawn. "homtom.quiet" is no longer parsed (quiet is the default).
 - Boot prints "homtom: LCD console muted, bootloader frame adopted" (or
   "not adopted" / "verbose") for the device check.
 - homtom_splash 1 while muted draws nothing (the GUI mute no longer
   repaints the splash); 0 unmutes under console_lock, clears the screen and
   redraws the newest log lines that fit, then continues live.
 - Boot guard: if nothing has written homtom_splash 60 s after boot, the
   console unmutes and prints "homtom: boot incomplete: ...".
 - The oops/panic paths are unchanged: the first console write with
   oops_in_progress clears the screen and turns the panel on, and the kmsg
   dumper redraws the incident and freezes the console.

Applies with -p1 after 0006 (tree .runtime/linux-trim-k3 -> linux-trim-k4).
No .config change.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/compressed/misc.c
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/compressed/misc.c
@@ -133,7 +133,47 @@
 
 extern int do_decompress(u8 *input, int len, u8 *output, void (*error)(char *x));
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_MACH_TOMTOMGO
+/*
+ * homtom GO 630: TTBL leaves its splash on screen in a buffer at 0x30400000, and the kernel Image inflates over it (kernel
+ * text there shows as coloured noise). Copy the frame the LCD is showing into the buffer the kernel keeps reserved
+ * (0x33F00000) and point the LCD DMA at it before inflating. Both buffers then hold the same pixels, so the switch is
+ * invisible. Nothing changes when the LCD is off, already scans 0x33F00000, or any value is out of range.
+ */
+#define HOMTOM_LCD		0x4D000000UL
+#define HOMTOM_FB_PHYS		0x33F00000UL
+#define HOMTOM_FB_MAX		0x40000UL
 
+extern void *memcpy(void *dest, const void *src, size_t n);
+
+static void homtom_adopt_fb(unsigned long free_end)
+{
+	volatile u32 *lcd = (volatile u32 *)HOMTOM_LCD;
+	u32 s1 = lcd[5], s2 = lcd[6];
+	unsigned long src = (unsigned long)(s1 & 0x3fffffff) << 1;
+	unsigned long bytes = (unsigned long)((s2 - s1) & 0x1fffff) << 1;
+	unsigned long p;
+
+	if (!(lcd[0] & 1) || src == HOMTOM_FB_PHYS)
+		return;
+	if (!bytes || bytes > HOMTOM_FB_MAX || src < 0x30000000UL || src + bytes > 0x34000000UL)
+		return;
+	if (src < HOMTOM_FB_PHYS + HOMTOM_FB_MAX && src + bytes > HOMTOM_FB_PHYS)
+		return;
+	if (free_end > HOMTOM_FB_PHYS)
+		return;
+
+	memcpy((void *)HOMTOM_FB_PHYS, (const void *)src, bytes);
+	/* RAM is write-back cacheable here: clean the copy (ARMv4 clean D line by MVA, VA == PA) and drain the write buffer. */
+	for (p = HOMTOM_FB_PHYS; p < HOMTOM_FB_PHYS + bytes; p += 32)
+		asm volatile("mcr p15, 0, %0, c7, c10, 1" : : "r" (p) : "memory");
+	asm volatile("mcr p15, 0, %0, c7, c10, 4" : : "r" (0) : "memory");
+
+	lcd[5] = HOMTOM_FB_PHYS >> 1;
+	lcd[6] = ((HOMTOM_FB_PHYS >> 1) + (bytes >> 1)) & 0x1fffff;
+}
+#endif
+
